Template: @PACKAGE@/name
Type: string
Default: @DEFAULT_NAME@
Description: Name of a backend instance to create now:
 Its DEFAULT_PREFIX, which names /etc/bcc/<name>, /var/lib/bcc/<name>, the
 @BINARY@@<name> service and the backend in MSS. Leave it empty to create
 none; `sudo @BINARY@-provision <name>` creates one at any time.

Template: @PACKAGE@/executor
Type: select
Choices: @EXECUTORS@
Default: @DEFAULT_EXECUTOR@
Description: Executor of the instance:

Template: @PACKAGE@/port
Type: string
Default: @DEFAULT_PORT@
Description: Port the instance serves on:
 Each instance on this machine needs its own.

Template: @PACKAGE@/mss_url
Type: string
Default: http://localhost:8002
Description: URL of MSS:

Template: @PACKAGE@/redis
Type: select
Choices-C: local, url
Choices: local Redis, existing Redis
Default: local
Description: Redis for the job queues:

Template: @PACKAGE@/redis_url
Type: string
Default: redis://redis.example.com:6379/0
Description: URL of the existing Redis, without its password:
 With its ACL user if it has one, e.g. redis://bcc@redis.example.com:6379/0.
 The password is asked next.

Template: @PACKAGE@/redis_password
Type: password
Description: Password of the Redis user:
 Stored only in the instance's backend.env, which root and the bcc account
 alone can read. Leave it empty if Redis has none.
